{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016345-2e-mage-sight-and-mysteries","id":1016345,"title":"[2e] Mage Sight and Mysteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T18:24:21-08:00","id":1016345,"title":"[2e] Mage Sight and Mysteries","content":"So I'm brand new to 2e, and would like some clarifications on how Mysteries and Mage Sight interact (particularly in relation to Awakened spells).<br /> <br /> Peripheral Mage Sight:<br /> Pings on any active magical effect.<br /> <br /> Active Mage Sight:<br /> Sees phenomena in relation to the Arcanum used (Object structure, durability, value, quality), supernatural effects in relation to the Arcanum, and Awakened spells being cast (from any Arcanum).<br /> Does AMS also reveal if someone is Awakened?<br /> <br /> Focused Mage Sight:<br /> Sees a particular phenomenon through a particular Arcanum. Neither Revelation and Scrutiny appear to actually inform the Awakened which spell it is.<br /> <br /> So for an example that has come up in our first session:<br /> <br /> A corpse's appearance has been changed by a Corpse Mask spell hiding a stab wound as an electrical burn.<br /> When the spell is cast, it pings on Peripheral - and continues to ping because it is still Active.<br /> The mages go out, a Death/Matter and Prime/Forces going into Active Mage Sight.<br /> Both can see the presence of the spell (it is a Death spell, and Prime can see Awakened magic).<br /> Forces sight simply shows the burn wounds which the corpse has been masked to look like.<br /> A death mage attempts Forensic Gaze, provoking a Clash of Wills against the Corpse Mask, and fails, simply getting that the person died from electrical burns.<br /> (This also pings the PMS of all the group, and forces a Tilt upon all mages in AMS)<br /> The Death Mage attempts a Revelation on the Mystery, discovering that it is Death Awakened magic, the signature nimbus is righteousness, that it is less than an hour old, and that it is Veiling.<br /> <br /> And that was about where we left it.<br /> Attempting a Scrutiny would give that the spell had been cast with a duration of a Month, that no Paradox was caused and that Death created the spell. (Do they find out what the spell does from a successful Scrutiny?)<br /> <br /> As I understand it, a Prime mage could also perform the Revelation and Scrutiny, but any mage without any of those two Arcanum could not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12722-youngy","name":"Youngy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T18:47:13-08:00","id":1016350,"title":"","content":"To the best of my knowledge, this is how all of this plays out Read As Worded. Of course, you're always free to give your players any info you want.<br /> <br /> Peripheral mage sight -- sixth sense, pings any time a supernatural effect activates nearby. AMS does not reveal if someone is awakened; I believe you need a prime 1 knowing effect for that.<br /> <br /> Corpse Mask is a Veiling effect. When cast, it would ping Peripheral mage sight -- however, it would <i>not</i> ping the mage's senses afterward until they turned on AMS for Death. The effect is active, however, it's not being activated beyond the round in which it is cast, it's sitting there.Once a mage turns on AMS for death, there would be a Clash of Wills with the spell, and the mage would instantly be aware that a Clash of Wills was occurring. If the mage wins, then Corpse Mask would not affect them. (To my knowledge, this does not tell the Mage what they overpowered with their Clash of Wills, just that whatever it was, they broke through it.)<br /> <br /> Forces sight wouldn't really reveal much here, I don't think. I wouldn't even include burn marks, myself. &quot;nothing beyond what your physical, mundane eyes can see.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do believe that the Forensic Gaze would Clash of Wills with the Corpse Mask, yes. If the Forensic Gaze fails, the mage would see whatever the Corpse Mask dictates. The act of casting a spell does ping the Peripheral sights of all mages nearby. I do not believe the Clash of Wills, nor the Corpse Mask, does.<br /> <br /> Revelation with Death Sight would say &quot;It is Awakened magic.&quot; If the Corpse Mask was not a rote, it would also say &quot;Death magic,&quot; and give the Signiture Nimbus of the mage who cast the spell. Either way, the Revelation would indicate how long it had been since the spell was cast. Optionally, you can include that it is Veiling.<br /> <br /> Scrutiny is where you get a little more control over what information is being given.<br /> <br /> You could tell the players the signature nimbus of the caster now, if it was a Rote (or an Attainment). Interestingly, this seems to indicate that if the spell was a Rote, the players don't learn what Arcana it was from (see Surface Information, p 94 -- compare with Deep Information, same page.)<br /> <br /> You can tell the players the spell factors (any information related to Duration, Potency, Scale -- I also believe technically the casting speed and casting range, as those are considered 'factors' in the quick-casting guide in the back of the book), whether it caused Paradox, and whether or not the spell has been relinquished.<br /> <br /> It does not seem to indicate that mages can learn the exact nature of the spell's effects; that much appears to be left to the players to deduce. They could also dispel the effect to see what changes, but that's the only way I can think of to prove factually the exact nature of the spell's effects.<br /> <br /> I am uncertain about the Prime or Death vs. other Arcana question. I'm not entirely certain you can use Prime to Scrutinize a Death effect to that extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}